  "projects/infer.md": "# `infer` — From-Scratch Local Hybrid Inference Engine\n\nRepo: [github.com/eosterloh/infer](https://github.com/eosterloh/infer) · July–August 2026 (ongoing) · Python, C++, CUDA, PyTorch.\n\nPlug-and-play local inference engine built for agents and model experiments: drop in a HuggingFace checkpoint folder (`config.json` + safetensors or GGUF) and generate greedy or sampled tokens (`temperature`, `top_k`, `top_p`, `seed`) with exact greedy-decode logit parity against HuggingFace.\n\n## Capabilities\n- **30+ model families**: Dense, MoE, and hybrid SSM / DeltaNet architectures including Llama (1–4), Mistral / Mixtral, Qwen2 / Qwen3 / Qwen3.5 / Qwen3.8, DeepSeek V2/V3, Gemma 1–3, Phi 3/4, OLMo, Jamba (Mamba-1/2), Qwen Gated DeltaNet, and Nemotron-H (Nano + Super LatentMoE). North star: **Nemotron NVFP4 fused on DGX Spark**.\n- **Multimodal & speculative decode**: Vision towers (Qwen2.5-VL / Qwen3.5, Gemma3, Llama 4, Mistral3) and native Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) draft layers.\n- **Byte-level JSON Schema constrained decoding**: Pushdown JSON-schema matcher (`json_schema=` / `generate_json`) guaranteeing valid schema-conformant tool calls for agent loops like `lab`, with `last_json_stats` reporting whether token budget forced early closure.\n- **Custom CUDA kernels on DGX Spark (`sm_121`)**: Custom `torch.ops.infer.*` extension (`rms_norm`, `fused_add_rms_norm`, `rope_inplace`, `act_mul`, `gemv` / `qgemv`, `dequant`, online-softmax `attn_decode`, `moe_gemv` / `qmoe_gemv`, `mamba2_scan`, `gdn_decode`), CUDA graph capture, and INT4 / NVFP4 / FP8 weight packing with automatic PyTorch fallback.\n",
  "projects/openclaw.md": "# Openclaw Fork & Local RAG Experiments\n\nRepos: [github.com/eosterloh/openclaw-fork](https://github.com/eosterloh/openclaw-fork) · [github.com/eosterloh/PageIndexOllamaRag](https://github.com/eosterloh/PageIndexOllamaRag) · 2026.\n\n- **`openclaw-fork`**: Personal agent runtime fork adding built-in telemetry and LangChain integration as an observable companion to the personal MCP / dossier stack.\n- **`PageIndexOllamaRag`**: Reasoning-based, vectorless document-index RAG adapted to run against local Ollama models.\n",
  "projects/rsi.md": "# TinyTrains / `lab` — RSI & Auto-research Harness\n\nRepo: [github.com/eosterloh/lab](https://github.com/eosterloh/lab) · July–August 2026 · Python, PyTorch, LangSmith.\n\nLong-running recursive self-improvement (RSI) / auto-research agent harness for an **8M-parameter** Llama-style model trained on TinyStories under a **3.5-day** compute budget.\n\n## Loop & Safety Architecture\n- **Phased loop**: `Eval (read-only) → Research (sandboxed web/code/data, budgeted) → Train (GPU-locked commit from a hashed pack) → Eval`.\n- **Anti-reward-hacking promotion gate**: Frozen eval (`core v1`) and promotion are NOT policy tools. Promotion is gated on **`confirm_ppl`** (held-out perplexity on a frozen split the policy cannot write), alongside tune/OOD PPL and mini benchmark slices (HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, PIQA).\n- **Hypothesis & Episode memory**: `enter_train` refuses until `hypothesis.json` (claim, falsification criteria, checklist) and a hashed pack are valid. Every completed cycle writes an episode card under `episodes/` and updates `beliefs.md`.\n- **Constrained experimenter policy**: Runs an experimenter policy (default `Qwen3.8-27B`) through `infer` using byte-level JSON Schema constrained decoding so every turn emits a valid phase-scoped `{\"tool\", \"args\"}` call, traced locally to `trace.jsonl` (with optional LangSmith mirroring).\n",
  "projects/training.md": "# `training` — From-Scratch ~20M PyTorch Language Model\n\nRepo: [github.com/eosterloh/training](https://github.com/eosterloh/training) · September 2026 · Python, PyTorch, DGX Spark.\n\nFrom-scratch ~20M-parameter language model pretraining stack on DGX Spark (`h=384, L=10, i=1152, 8 heads`) trained on **FineWeb-Edu** with a fresh 32k BPE tokenizer.\n\n- Every core block is written by hand as `nn.Module`s (`RMSNorm`, `RoPE`, causal attention, `SwiGLU`, residual connections, MoE router + load-balance loss) without `transformers.LlamaForCausalLM` or `nn.MultiheadAttention`.\n- Controlled architecture ablations on an identical token budget and seed: dense `MHA → GQA → MQA → sliding-window attention → top-2 MoE`, tracking validation loss from chance (`~10.4`) down below `5.0` (`~4.5` target).\n",
